/*
    `^^` carries no meaning of its own: it is `^` with its operands reversed, so it is
    defined for exactly the signatures `^` is defined for.
    On numeric operands `10 ^^ 2` therefore denotes `2 ^ 10`.
    The reversal is only about which operand is written first, which is what lets the
    function-set reading put the domain on the left.
*/

10 ^^ 2
